16. Disclosures in Offer Document
(1) The offer document shall contain all material disclosures which are true,
correct and adequate to enable the investors to take an informed investment
decision.
(2) For the purpose of `materiality' of disclosure under this regulation, the
issuer shall provide the details of its `materiality policy', wherever
applicable, in the offer document and ensure the disclosure of all material
information post filing of offer document and prior to listing.
